► ANSWER                                                                        

Reading the failing bar, the defect is precise: --allow-hand-times currently    
suppresses the refusal for every entry in hand, including the entries           
Call.hand_time_entries() synthesises from a server Date header /                
response.created when the logger stamped nothing. Those are not hand-entered    
values, so the switch must not reach them. The no-switch path (which refuses    
them as hand-time and must stay byte-identical for A3a/A3b/T7b) is left alone;  
under the switch they become the time refusal the bar asks for, naming the log  
and every unstamped call.                                                       

The change is confined to kit/emit_custody.py: evaluator_history() gains        
allow_hand and, after flag_calls, refuses each unstamped evaluator call's       
synthesised entry with kind time. That is the same Refusals mechanism already   
used for "a model evaluator with no harness log", and it leaves maker logs,     
typed hand times, and every other refusal untouched. kit/custody_history.py     
needs no change — it already distinguishes the sources.                         

